      "connectsTo": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/460169769",
      "details": "<p>The Anu Gate, the fifth of the eight city gates of D\u016br-\u0160arruk\u012bn mentioned in Sargon II\u2019s royal inscriptions, might be identified as undecorated Khorsabad Gate 7, the southernmost entrance on the northwest wall.</p>\r\n<p>Because there is no one-to-one correlation between Sargon\u2019s inscriptions and available archaeological evidence, the proposed identification of the Anu Gate with Khorsabad Gate 7 remains open to debate. Alternative locations have been suggested: decorated <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/460169768\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Gate 6</a> and grand <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/344172035\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Citadel Gate B</a>. Because one expects a plain gate to be named after Anu, Gate 7 seems to be the most plausible suggested location for the Anu Gate, especially since the listing of the gates of D\u016br-\u0160arruk\u012bn in textual sources is counterclockwise around the city, starting with the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/344172036\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">\u0160ama\u0161 Gate</a>, which has been tentatively identified as decorated <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/918508895\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Gate 3</a>.</p>",
